  "steps": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large saucepan over a medium heat. Add the onion, red bell pepper and carrot, then cook for 8–10 minutes, stirring often, until softened and the onion is translucent.",
    "Add the garlic, cumin, chilli powder and paprika. Cook for 1 minute, stirring, until fragrant.",
    "Stir in the cocoa powder and tomato paste, coating the vegetables well, and cook for 1–2 minutes until the paste darkens slightly.",
    "Add the canned tomatoes, black beans, kidney beans, chickpeas, vegetable stock, sweetcorn, salt and black pepper. Stir well and bring to a gentle boil.",
    "Reduce the heat and simmer uncovered for 25–30 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the chilli is thick and the vegetables are tender. If it gets too thick, add a splash of water.",
    "Stir in the lime juice, taste and adjust the salt or chilli powder if needed. Scatter with chopped coriander before serving."
  ],
